<?xml version="1.0"?>
<rdf:RDF xmlns="http://w3id.org/daselab/onto/spatiotemporalextent#"
     xml:base="http://w3id.org/daselab/onto/spatiotemporalextent"
     xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"
     xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#"
     xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
     xmlns:xml="http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace"
     xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#"
     xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#"
     xmlns:skos="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#"
     xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/"
     xmlns:spatime="http://w3id.org/daselab/onto/spatiotemporalextent#"
     xmlns:cpannotationschema="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#">
    <owl:Ontology rdf:about="http://w3id.org/daselab/onto/spatiotemporalextent">
        <owl:imports rdf:resource="http://w3id.org/daselab/onto/trajectory"/>
        <owl:imports rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl"/>
        <dc:creator>Adila Krisnadhi, Pascal Hitzler</dc:creator>
        <dcterms:description rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">This pattern models a spatiotemporal extent, i.e., a combination of spatial and temporal extent as a set of generalized trajectories which cannot have temporal overlap. This pattern reuses semantic trajectory pattern as component.</dcterms:description>
        <dcterms:title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Spatiotemporalextent Pattern</dcterms:title>
        <cpannotationschema:coversRequirements>Where is Poland located in 1700?, 
List all places and time in which the 1990 World Chess Championship Match take place.,
Where and when did the oceanographic cruise A01132 go?</cpannotationschema:coversRequirements>
        <cpannotationschema:hasComponent rdf:resource="http://ontologydesignpatterns.org/wiki/Submissions:Trajectory"/>
        <cpannotationschema:hasComponent rdf:resource="http://w3id.org/daselab/onto/trajectory"/>
        <cpannotationschema:hasComponent>Trajectory</cpannotationschema:hasComponent>
        <cpannotationschema:hasIntent rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">This pattern models a spatiotemporal extent, i.e., a combination of spatial and temporal extent as a set of generalized trajectories which cannot have temporal overlap. This pattern reuses semantic trajectory pattern as component.</cpannotationschema:hasIntent>
        <cpannotationschema:relatedCPs>Trajectory</cpannotationschema:relatedCPs>
        <cpannotationschema:scenarios>The World Chess Championship Match 1990 was held in two parts: New York (October 8 to November 7) and Lyons - France (November 26 to December 30).

The Renaissance occured in different places at different times.

A hurricane moves through the spacetime.</cpannotationschema:scenarios>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Curated by OntoBoard 1.155.0, so that the pattern passes ODK&apos;s quality report with its default profile, names every term with a label, and is consistent and coherent. Changes: label added x10; term declared x8;
- header: dcterms:title &quot;Spatiotemporalextent Pattern&quot; - the library&apos;s name for the pattern
- header: dcterms:description - the library&apos;s description of the pattern
- file: pattern.owl declares &lt;http://w3id.org/daselab/onto/trajectory#Trajectory&gt; as a class, as pattern.ttl did
Each change is listed under &quot;curated&quot; in the pattern&apos;s metadata.json in OntoBoard&apos;s pattern library.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Ontology>
    


